{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31ba-708f-bd53-3eeb1b384a21","id":"01a1a62b-8756-7341-97cd-06fdf903f3c7","idempotency_key":"f7a9d626702035fc390e95d068de622fe7bfa763ba95c89b236610f02a857a5e","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T10:47:12Z","payload":{"note":"Glicko-2 ratings, built to the ratings contract in 40-play-arena-ratings.md rather than invented. crates/ai/src/glicko.rs is the algorithm (Glickman 2013) with the paper's worked example as a test - 1500/200/0.06 against 1400, 1550, 1700 produces 1464.06 / 151.52 / 0.05999, asserted to 0.05 and 0.00001. A period is applied once from the whole period, and one test asserts period != sequential application, because that distinction is the whole point of the period. Rules: only model-versus-model games under standard-v1 are rateable and each exclusion says why it was excluded (human, casual, tool-assisted, aborted, provider-failed); competitor ids carry the model version so a bump is a new competitor; conservative rank is rating - 2*RD; an engine anchor sits at its nominal Elo with a 50 deviation and its own row never moves while its opponents still feel the game. Storage is rbc-db schema v7 (rating_games, rating_ledger, ratings, rating_anchors) and the period logic is in rbc-ai, split along the dependency direction because rbc-db does not depend on rbc-ai. The ledger holds a before/after row per side per period and 'ratings' is only a cache: rebuild() replays every period and a test asserts it reproduces the cache exactly, for a three-period ladder and for a three-game tournament period. 18 tests; workspace tests and clippy -D warnings clean on both feature sets. Not built: a route or UI for the leaderboard (t-a488) - this ticket is the machinery.","target":"t-2bbf"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
